Conversation Summary
The team is pivoting from a failed $2M Epicor Kinetic implementation back to a modernized CMS/AS400 layer, using AI and wearable tech to automate manual data entry, resolve 100% inventory inaccuracies, and integrate IHS Global forecasting to recover lost automotive program revenue.
• ERP Strategy Pivot and Epicor Implementation Challenges
◦ Context: The team is navigating a transition from legacy AS400 and failed Epicor Kinetic systems to a more efficient, AI-integrated workflow to address data integrity and manual entry bottlenecks.
◦ Strategic Pivot to Epicor CMS: Abandoning Kinetic due to excessive customization needs; returning to the "brilliant" automotive CMS version. Total Epicor spend reached $2M with minimal support and high legal/contractual friction.
◦ System Integration and Cloud Strategy: Utilizing a SaaS model to allow AI layering on top of the database. The backend database is the critical foundation for all technical setups and future system replacements.
◦ EDI Implementation Failures: Epicor native EDI failed for automotive requirements (GM), forcing a $500k secondary implementation via Autocore/AIM. Existing quarterly service contracts ($70k) provide no value.
 
• Inventory Management and Operational Inefficiencies
◦ Context: Current reliance on manual "machine sheets" and disconnected office data entry results in "inventory hell" and 100% data inaccuracy.
◦ Financial Reconciliation Crisis: Weekly calls required to fix COGS; items pull from wrong bins (Bin 1 vs Bin 2). Manual journal entries and "fake jobs" are used to achieve month-end net-zero balances.
◦ Manual Data Entry Burden: Staff spend 20+ hours weekly "massaging" data. Users sidestep the "garbage" UI, which requires 2-3 extra clicks per PO, leading to further data corruption.
◦ WIP and Labor Discrepancies: System puts labor into WIP in ways that prevent reconciliation. Month-end requires a 45-minute total plant stoppage to capture a 1,400-page manual inventory snapshot.
 
• AI Automation and Wearable Technology Integration
◦ Context: Strategy to use AI as a non-disruptive "concrete filler" for process cracks, eventually replacing the foundation over three years.
◦ Workforce Automation and Headcount: Evaluating headcount reduction (Charlie, Tammy, Amy) via AI. Successfully in-sourced $10k/month of external services using 24/7 automated systems.
◦ Wearable Voice-to-Data Systems: Implementing smart glasses (Reality 2) and transcription pins to convert verbal worker narration into structured system data, eliminating physical machine sheets.
◦ Deterministic vs. Probabilistic Logic: Strict rule: No AI for "right/wrong" logic. AI is used only to generate 10,000+ lines of deterministic code in minutes, shortcutting 90% of development.
 
• Demand Forecasting and Automotive Market Strategy
◦ Context: Transitioning from a 6-week to a 16-week forecast horizon to stabilize production and procurement.
◦ IHS Global Data Integration: Integrating IHS Global forecasts to align awarded POs with market trends. Critical for recovering from a $4.2M GM program cancellation due to EV market shifts.
◦ Capacity Modeling and Throughput: Factory operates at 51% capacity ($16M-$17M revenue) with a theoretical max of 80% ($32M). AI tools translated 1980s ladder logic to increase engineering throughput.
◦ Inventory Min-Max Optimization: Only 15.8% of inventory has set levels. New system uses four algorithms (smooth, erratic, inverted, lumpy) to recommend levels across 100% of stock.
 
• Manufacturing Processes and Infrastructure Security
◦ Context: Overview of specialized plastic molding (EPS/EPP) and the underlying IT security protecting proprietary manufacturing data.
◦ Specialized Product Lines: Focus on high-density medical coolers (0% spoilage over 3 days) and Cadillac Celestiq bumper cores. EPP used for automotive; EPS for building materials (ICF).
◦ ICF Structural Benefits: Insulated Concrete Forms (ICF) provide fire/tornado resistance and extreme energy efficiency ($40/month for 20k sq ft). Curing in forms makes concrete 2x harder.
◦ Triple-Layered Security and Backups: Triple-redundant backups in NYC/DC ($400/mo). Onsite Azure servers sync Epicor data every 15 minutes to mitigate "DPC crash" risks and external cyber threats.
 
 
